  "name": "Ganju (Jiangxi opera)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Opera of northeastern Jiangxi, from the Raohe (Poyang) and Guangxin troupe traditions, joined under the name Ganju in the 1950s; it keeps the old Yiyang high-tune style, in which one singer leads and others take up the line over gongs and drums without strings, alongside tanqiang tunes accompanied by a huqin fiddle (the erhu card stands in) and other strings. It entered China's national intangible heritage list in 2006.",
